# Patterns scripts/package_release.py excludes from the runtime release
# bundle (dist/ai-friend-runtime.tar.gz / .zip), on top of its RUNTIME_FILES /
# RUNTIME_DIRS whitelist. gitignore-style: one pattern per line, "#" comments.
#
# This exists as defense-in-depth, not the primary control -- the packager
# only ever copies what RUNTIME_DIRS names, so nothing here should normally
# matter. It matters the moment RUNTIME_DIRS is edited without this file in
# mind: personal/ was whitelisted in RUNTIME_DIRS for one release and shipped
# the author's real persona (name, biography) into a committed, public
# tarball. This list is the backstop for the next time that whitelist changes.

personal/
audit/
AUDIT.md
academic_benchmarks/
website/
node_modules/
.next/
target/
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.tar.gz
*.zip
.DS_Store
